		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4895&amp;p=35846#p35846"><![CDATA[
Hi, I'm trying to follow step1 of the OpenGD-77 installation procedure and update the original firmware first (on my Radioddity GD77) to latest 4.3.9.sgl (from 3.02.01 installed) -before installing OpenGD-77. Pluging the cable on my win10 pc, putting the radio in DFU mode but when I try to hit "Download"for the update to begin "No Device found"error appears. The cable I use looks like this one: <a href="https://www.radioddity.com/products/programming-cable-for-tyt-md-380-md-390-md-680-radioddity-gd-77-gd-77s?srsltid=AfmBOorR8gV-mZxGrWtktaUQW07w6hFp8Ai56gYPaMIOx3pskCd7USPi&amp;fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAAR0_C17zeowdBUhF4ozh7ZvnHKWgIxXNLNaa61ahL2OESO7ZXHrOe_95__0_aem_SM1IgKiYcth7-pCjqevg5A" class="postlink">https://www.radioddity.com/products/pro ... -pCjqevg5A</a>. (I'm not 100% sure if this is the correct cable as the previous owner of the radio -which by the way is in prestine/like new condition- could not confirm if this was in the package when the radio was bought or is from an other radio he had). Attached the photo of the cable I have. When the cable is pluged in to USB(even if the radio is not attached on the other side), in device manager I can see that it's there and appears as: Prolific USB-to-Serial Comm Port (COM5) -COM5 is also the port I choose during the update process. So this is a USB cable clearly with a chip on it. Some fellow hams insisted that this is not the correct cable and that the right one is just a USB "fossil"without any chip on it. So MY QUESTION (at last <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> ): Can any body please confirm which is the correct cable for updating the -original- (not OpenGD77) firmware? If the cable is not the problem then what should I double-check?? Any advice / help would be appreciated. Thanks and 73' de SV2TBR<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2854&amp;sid=7c51030e026555a6bb894c1f1f779923" class="postimage" alt="01.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8136">SV2TBR</a> — Thu Feb 20, 2025 9:09 am</p><hr />
